Python Dice Game 🎲

About the Project

This is a two-player dice game written in Python. Players take turns rolling a virtual dice. Rolling an even number earns one point, while rolling an odd number resets the player's score. The player with the most points at the end wins.

Features

Random dice rolls using Python's random module.

Two-player scoring system.

Even and odd number detection using the modulo operator (%).

Option to roll again or end a turn.

Option to play another round.

