Challenges and Solutions

Challenge 1: The game would not stop when I entered "no".

The problem was that I used == instead of = when asking the player whether they wanted to play again.

I learnt that == compares two values, whereas = assigns a value to a variable. Changing the operator allowed the program to save the player's answer and end the game correctly.

Challenge 2: Handling different capitalisations of user input.

I used .lower() on the input so that answers such as Yes, YES and yes would be treated consistently.

How to Run

Install Python 3.

Download or clone this repository.

Run the Python file from a terminal:

python dice_game.py

